{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775510972,"nonce":"pv6gz2kUrE+QYL15Rj9i4SXcGME=","title":"Parse MCP signal tool calls in Claude Code adapter","message":"Parse MCP signal tool calls in Claude Code adapter\n\n## Context\nSignal protocol Phase 1b: wire MCP signal detection into ClaudeCodeAgent._parse(). The MCP server is shipped by the previous issue (02c5e70). Claude Code emits tool_use events with names like mcp__nightshift-signals__nightshift_done. Also add --mcp-config flag to the start() command.\n\nDepends on: 02c5e70\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_stream_parser.py::test_mcp_signal_done_emits_done_marker\n  Assert: a tool_use event with name \"mcp__nightshift-signals__nightshift_done\" and input {\"summary\": \"task done\"} produces AgentEvent with content \"@@DONE@@\"\n- tests/test_stream_parser.py::test_mcp_signal_checkpoint_emits_checkpoint_marker\n  Assert: a tool_use event with name \"mcp__nightshift-signals__nightshift_checkpoint\" and input {\"description\": \"progress\"} produces AgentEvent with content \"@@CHECKPOINT@@ progress\"\n- tests/test_stream_parser.py::test_mcp_signal_question_emits_question_marker\n  Assert: a tool_use event with name \"mcp__nightshift-signals__nightshift_question\" and input {\"question\": \"what next?\"} produces two AgentEvents: \"@@QUESTION@@ what next?\" then \"@@WAITING@@\"\n- tests/test_stream_parser.py::test_non_signal_mcp_tool_parsed_as_tool_call\n  Assert: a tool_use event with name \"mcp__other-server__some_tool\" is parsed as TOOL_CALL (not a signal)\n- tests/test_stream_parser.py::test_start_includes_mcp_config_flag\n  Assert: when MCP config path exists at /opt/nightshift/mcp-config.json, start() includes --mcp-config flag in the command\n\n## Files\n- adapters/agents/claude_code.py (modify — update _parse_assistant_content and start)\n- core/constants.py (modify — add MCP_CONFIG_CONTAINER_PATH, MCP_SIGNAL_SERVER_PREFIX)\n\n## Implementation\n1. In core/constants.py, add:\n   - `MCP_CONFIG_CONTAINER_PATH = \"/opt/nightshift/mcp-config.json\"`\n   - `MCP_SIGNAL_SERVER_PREFIX = \"mcp__nightshift-signals__\"`\n2. In ClaudeCodeAgent._parse_assistant_content(), before the existing tool_use handling:\n   - Check if tool name starts with MCP_SIGNAL_SERVER_PREFIX\n   - Extract signal name (nightshift_done/nightshift_checkpoint/nightshift_question)\n   - For done: yield AgentEvent(TEXT, \"@@DONE@@\")\n   - For checkpoint: yield AgentEvent(TEXT, f\"@@CHECKPOINT@@ {input.get('description', '')}\")\n   - For question: yield AgentEvent(TEXT, f\"@@QUESTION@@ {input.get('question', '')}\") then yield AgentEvent(TEXT, \"@@WAITING@@\")\n   - Otherwise: fall through to existing tool_use handling\n3. In ClaudeCodeAgent.start(), if Path(MCP_CONFIG_CONTAINER_PATH).exists(), add [\"--mcp-config\", MCP_CONFIG_CONTAINER_PATH] to cmd\n\n## Patterns to follow\nSee existing tool_use handling in _parse_assistant_content() at adapters/agents/claude_code.py:185-190.\nSee docs/signal-protocol-design.md \"Claude Code\" section for event format.\n\nREQ: REQ-004","files":null}]}